A||N||17||carpetviper||NEED HELP NOW!!!||||4||
Z||000000||carpetviper||11-22-2001||02:27 PM||||Okay this is the deal. I have a '86 V6 SE and it is losing oil, but only when driving at 65 or more (interstate) and before shifting, never really reved above 3k. My oil seems to stay pretty okay when just driving to school or so at 55-60mph. Also there is black soot in 3 out of 4 exhaust tips and I can see a little bit of water droplets after startup in the exhaust tips. BTW I just changed the oil and flushed it about 2 weeks ago. Any help you guys can give would be great.  <p>[This message has been edited by carpetviper (edited 11-27-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000001||StuGood||11-22-2001||05:25 PM||||Not sure, but I would start by checking your PCV system (check hoses for obstructions, and replace the PCV valve).  Hope this helps  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ||||reg||5
Z||000002||carpetviper||11-22-2001||05:53 PM||||Well, I just ordered one, we'll see if it helps any.<P>BTW i just added my sig.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/carpetviper/carpetviper.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000003||carpetviper||11-22-2001||05:57 PM||||Here I fixed it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpetviper.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by carpetviper (edited 11-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||carpetviper||11-22-2001||07:36 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> Can anyone out there help me out?<p>[This message has been edited by carpetviper (edited 11-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||11-22-2001||07:57 PM||||If you mean you are losing oil out of the engine, my first suggestion is to replace the distributor o-ring. These get old, and allow oil to make it past, particularly at higher rpm.||||reg||1
Z||000006||carpetviper||11-22-2001||10:01 PM||||How is oil going to get into the distributor?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Mach10||11-22-2001||10:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by carpetviper:<BR><B>How is oil going to get into the distributor?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Not INTO the distributer, but up and out the distributer shaft... That *IS* a common problem  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||10
Z||000008||carpetviper||11-23-2001||11:32 AM||||Well I talked to my mechanic today and he said that by the black soot in the exhaust tips he thinks that my engines burning rich. Maybe a O2 sensor, What do you think? About the oil, they suppose that a big part of it might be the valve seals. Thats what i thought too. Should I go for that or wait and save for a remanufactured motor?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpetviper.jpg"> ||||reg||3
Z||000009||GodSend||11-23-2001||02:12 PM||||Change the dist. o-ring .. it will only cost a few bucks.  If you are careful and mark everything you should be able to get the timing reasonabily close ...||||reg||1
Z||000010||fiero56||11-23-2001||07:41 PM||||Valve-seals...that's classic <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">. Are you burning oil or dripping oil? If your dripping oil, and your mechanic is blaming valve-seals, its time to find someone else. This dude is full of $hit.<P>If your running rich, O2 sensor can cause it, so can engine temp sensor, vac leak, and any other host of things can cause you to run rich. What kind of mileage are you getting? <BR>I've got sooty exahust tips, and I always clear 32-33mpg+ highway, and mid 20's city with my 2.8 5-speed.||||reg||1
Z||000011||carpetviper||11-23-2001||11:14 PM||||If it was the distributor o-ring, wouldn't oil be noticable running down the side of the distributor shaft? Also, I'm pretty sure its burning off oil, because I haven't noticed any oil spots after parking anywhere, unless it only leaks while driving, but that doesn't make much sense. In this case it might me the valve seals, or the O-rings maybe. <BR>BTW, i'm getting approx. 28-30 mpg overall.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpetviper.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by carpetviper (edited 11-23-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000012||fiero56||11-24-2001||09:09 AM||||If the dist o-ring is bad, you will not see oil running down the dist shaft. You will see oil running down the topside of your tranny though. <P>If your burning oil, I don't see how it is really rpm related. But, piston rings, valve seals, a head gaskter(unlikely), etc, can all cause that. If your burning oil, you will likely see blue smoke when the engine is running.||||reg||1
Z||000013||carpetviper||11-26-2001||09:00 PM||||   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">  Hey, guys, I may have figured why I'm running rich; my coolant gauge read 100 and didn't fluctuate much and I was going about 60-65 for at least 20 min. That can't be right! Also my SERVICE ENG SOON light came on until I stopped to get gas then it remained off. I would guess that my coolant temp sensor is fried, but tonight my gauge ran around 160(where it usually runs)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  Any other ideas? Could an overheating engine cause me to burn off oil somehow?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpetviper.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by carpetviper (edited 11-27-2001).]||||reg||4
